{# redistribute static (no 'subnets') only picks up statics that fall on a natural classful major-network
   boundary. 172.16.199.0/24 is a subnet of the classful 172.16.0.0/16, so it gets silently dropped - the command
   succeeds, nothing is logged, and the route just never shows up anywhere. One of the most-cited real OSPF
   redistribution gotchas. #}
{% if rollback %}
router ospf 1
 no redistribute static
no ip route {{ bug_prefix }} {{ bug_mask }} Null0
{% else %}
ip route {{ bug_prefix }} {{ bug_mask }} Null0
router ospf 1
 redistribute static metric 20 metric-type 2
{% endif %}
